  "body": "Closes #1329\nClaim: cloud/i1329-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1329-sonnet)\n\n**Problem.** The offline-save banner's ✕ (\"Fermer\") is a default-style icon-only button in an `HStack`: its hit region is the glyph alone (~16 pt), under the HIG 44 pt.\n\n**Cause.** No frame / content shape on the button's label (`ReaderOfflineSave.swift`, `OfflineSaveBanner`).\n\n**Change.** New `OfflineSaveCloseButton` (same technique as `GifSearchClearButton`, #1296): `.minimumHitRegion()` on the label, margins pulled back by a negative padding (`MinimumHitRegion.overhang`), so the banner keeps its height and the glyph its place. Leading reach is capped at the stack spacing (8 pt) so the region never covers the text. Default button style kept (look unchanged). Not #1351's bordered glass: that changes the look, which the issue forbids.\n\n**Tests** (`OfflineSaveCloseTouchTargetTests`, hosted, xSmall / large / accessibility5): region ≥ 44×44; layout and glyph centre unchanged against the bare glyph; region's minX ≥ text's maxX. Red before the change by construction (`OfflineSaveCloseButton` did not exist, so the suite did not compile); not run here (Linux, no app build): to be seen green by the Compile check.\n\nDevice check owed (#893): tap just outside the ✕ closes the banner; tapping the message does not.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
