   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1): APPROVE** (head d8286aced7dff3515024b716a4ec97475019d775)\n\nThe diff matches its head and copies the pattern of `GifSearchClearButton` (#1296) line for line. The leading overhang is capped at the stack spacing, so the region never reaches the text. The negative padding gives the layout back, so the look stays the same: the default borderless style and the tint are unchanged, and `.labelStyle(.iconOnly)` moved onto the `Label`. Swift 6: the probes are `@MainActor` closures and `@State` is written from `onGeometryChange`, so isolation is fine. No line is over 140 characters.\n\nFindings (none blocking):\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Offline/OfflineSaveCloseTouchTargetTests.swift:52-87`. The tests host `OfflineSaveCloseButton` on its own. Before the fix they fail only because the type does not exist yet. If `OfflineSaveBanner` (`ReaderOfflineSave.swift:87`) goes back to the old `Button(\"Fermer\", systemImage:)`, all the tests stay green (LESSONS 2). They also do not check the region under `glassEffect` and `safeAreaBar`. Fix, optional, as for #1296: host `OfflineSaveBanner` with a saver in a done state, or add the in-situ tap to #893.\n2. **Detail**, `ReaderOfflineSave.swift:17` and `:120`. With a 16 pt glyph the vertical overhang is 14 pt. That is 6 pt above the glass, which is also above the top of the `safeAreaBar`, so the nav bar may take that band. It is 2 pt below, into the top edge of `LoadFailureBanner` (no outer top padding). \"Réessayer\" sits 12 pt inside its card, so it is not covered, but whether the full 44 pt is tappable needs a check on a device. Fix: add it to #893's device review.\n3. **Detail**. The default glyph size is 16, so the first frame lays out with that guess. That is harmless and the same as the precedent.\n\n**Checked**: compared the head diff with the given diff (identical). Read `MinimumHitRegion`, `GifSearchClearButton`, `GifSearchClearTouchTargetTests`, the banner's `safeAreaBar` placement and its neighbours in `TopicReaderView` (`LoadFailureBanner` inset, nav bar). Worked out the overhang against the paddings (16 h, 8 v, 4 bottom). Checked line lengths. Not run: an app build or the tests, which cannot run on Linux.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5). Author's answer: finding 1 accepted as a known limit, the in-situ tap goes to the #893 device check, since hosting `OfflineSaveBanner` needs a live `OfflineSaveModel` store and fetcher; findings 2 and 3 go to the same device check.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
